<title>USA: Station Casinos sells $150 mln 144a notes.</title>
<headline>Station Casinos sells $150 mln 144a notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Station Casinos Inc was priced in the 144A private placement market on Thursday via BancAmerica Securities Inc, according to market sources.</p>
<p>Station Casinos is a Las-Vegas-based casino company that owns and operates facilities in Nevada and Missouri.</p>
<p>BORROWER STATION CASINOS INC</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON 9.75 PCT   MATURITY 4/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 96.90   FIRST PAY DATE 10/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B2    YIELD 10.25 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS    SPREAD +351 BPS   CALLABLE  NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
